# Response headers for Cloudflare Pages.
#
# A CSP has to be a header, not a <meta http-equiv>: the meta form cannot carry
# frame-ancestors, and it applies only after the parser reaches it. Cloudflare serves
# this file's rules for every matching path, index.html included.
#
# Nothing here is observable locally — `vite preview` serves dist/ and ignores this
# file — so the only layer that can prove it arrived is the post-deploy smoke run.
# See docs/adr/0006-security.md.
#
# The policy is strict because the app earns it: one self-hosted module script, one
# compiled Tailwind stylesheet, no inline styles and no third-party scripts. Adding
# 'unsafe-inline' anywhere would give most of it back.
#
#   default-src 'self'    covers script-src and style-src by fallback
#   connect-src           the characters API, fetched with CORS
#   img-src               character portraits, plus the transparent data: gif
#                         CharacterImage swaps in while a retry is in flight
#   object-src 'none'     no <object>/<embed>, the classic injection surface
#   base-uri 'self'       stops an injected <base> re-pointing every relative URL
#   form-action 'none'    another directive with no default-src fallback; this app has
#                         no forms at all, so nothing is given up by closing the one
#                         exfiltration path an injected <form action=…> would use
#   frame-ancestors       clickjacking; X-Frame-Options repeats it for old browsers
#
# Caching is declared here too, because this file is the one place that controls it and
# leaving it to the host's defaults is a decision nobody wrote down. Vite emits
# content-hashed asset names, so those can be cached forever; the document that points
# at them cannot, or a deploy stays invisible until a browser decides to revalidate.
#
# `/*` and `/assets/*` both match an asset, and which Cache-Control wins is the host's
# rule rather than this file's — so tests/smoke/deployment.spec.ts asserts both after a
# real deploy rather than trusting the precedence.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://rickandmortyapi.com; img-src 'self' https://rickandmortyapi.com data:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
